{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"cinematic-untiring-dunnart","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# Context\n\nParent epic `a4bd-4ca8-c44f-49bb`. This is the behavior-changing story the epic exists for, and\nit lands LAST: it consumes the store from S1 (`248f-ac00-18db-4259`), the snapshot evidence from\nS2 (`83d3-61d9-fc59-424b`), and — critically — the upgrade backfill from S4\n(`f6e9-a5fd-e908-4b82`), without which the first post-upgrade pass would decline every legitimate\nremoval.\n\nThe defect: `managed_refs` is monotonic and marks a ref managed the instant it is created\nLOCALLY, so guard G3 (`inbound_differ.py::_diff_link_removals_inbound`) cannot distinguish a\nnever-pushed local link from a peer-deleted one. G4 (same-pass outbound-ADD suppression in\n`compute_inbound_mutations`) covers that blind spot ONLY when the outbound differ emits the\nre-ADD — but `outbound_links.py::_diff_links` dedups ADDs direction-agnostically on\n`(vendor_type, target_key)` and is \"intentionally NOT deduped on relation\", so a local link whose\nvendor type collides with an existing remote link in the OTHER direction (local `blocks` vs an\ninward `Blocks`, which reads as `depends_on`) is never pushed AND never G4-protected. Its removal\nrecord reaches the applier and removes a never-pushed local link.\n\n# Scope\n\n- `apply_inbound_records.py::_inbound_unlink_one`: before removing, consult the peer-confirmation\n  store. If the `(local_id, target_local_id, relation)` key is NOT confirmed, DECLINE: log a\n  WARNING naming the key and the reason, and return `False` (no write). The return value is\n  load-bearing — `False` keeps the silent-no-op canary in `apply_handlers.py` truthful.\n- Open the store once per pass, alongside the existing `_open_impossible_link_store(repo_root)`\n  in `_inbound_update_apply_links`, and thread it in — do not re-open per record.\n- The existing e39f behavior is preserved unchanged for confirmed links: removal stays\n  relation-scoped via `rebar.unlink(..., relation, ...)`, and a relation with no net-active local\n  link stays a logged INFO no-op.\n- Emit the per-pass decline count in the existing `_inbound_update_apply_links` INFO summary that\n  already reports impossible-link skips, so declines are operator-visible rather than log-only.\n- Tests are BEHAVIORAL, driven through `compute_inbound_mutations` and\n  `_inbound_update_apply_links` as the existing 2b16 suite does (it deliberately drives public\n  entry points, never a private helper by name).\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1 A removal record for a managed link with NO confirmation record is declined: no UNLINK\n      event is written, the link is still net-active locally, a WARNING is logged, and\n      `_inbound_unlink_one` returns False.\n- [ ] AC2 A removal record for a link WITH a confirmation record still converges — the link is\n      removed, exactly the named relation and no other.\n- [ ] AC3 The epic's motivating scenario end-to-end: a local `blocks` dep whose outbound ADD is\n      deduped by an inward same-vendor-type remote link is NOT removed by an inbound removal\n      record (this is the regression the epic names).\n- [ ] AC4 Re-applying the same declined record on a subsequent pass declines again idempotently\n      and writes nothing.\n- [ ] AC5 A backfill-sourced confirmation is sufficient for AC2 (no post-upgrade mass decline).\n- [ ] AC6 The per-pass INFO summary reports the decline count.\n- [ ] AC7 Mutation check: removing the confirmation check turns the AC1 and AC3 tests RED;\n      restoring it turns them GREEN. Recorded as a comment.\n- [ ] AC8 Every touched module stays under the 800-line cap (verify against `git archive HEAD`);\n      `make lint` and `make typecheck` clean; the existing\n      `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_inbound_link_removal_2b16.py` suite still passes.\n\n# Out of scope\n\nG3/G4 themselves are unchanged — the discrimination is added at the applier (G5) where the epic's\nAC places it. No change to `managed_refs` monotonicity. No change to the outbound ADD dedup key.","id":"47a0-7019-da4b-40e0","parent_id":"a4bd-4ca8-c44f-49bb","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Decline inbound removal of never-peer-confirmed links"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786558530994179001,"uuid":"573f581e-13c4-43d1-8b0e-f79056d925d5"}